Screens
=======

One file per screen in src/screens/. Route names are the strings registered in
src/navigation/.


Authentication stack
--------------------

SignInScreen        signin
	Email and password. On success the token pair is stored and AppShell
	swaps to the app stack.

SignUpScreen        signup
	Registration. Faculty and nationality are chosen here through
	components/auth/AuthSelect.js, which shows the faculty crest next to each
	option. Both values are required by the backend and both drive the
	student's avatar and leaderboard identity, so this is not a cosmetic
	step.

VerifyEmailScreen   verifyEmail
	Six digit email OTP, entered through components/auth/OtpInput.js.

ForgotPasswordScreen        forgot
ForgotPasswordOtpScreen     forgotVerify
ResetPasswordScreen         resetPassword
	The three step reset: request a code, verify it, set a new password.

SplashScreen and OnboardingScreen also exist in the folder. SplashScreen is
the branded hold. OnboardingScreen is not registered in any navigator; see
docs/maintenance.md.


Tabs
----

HomeScreen          home
	Greeting with the student's name and flag, the day streak, the Lancer
	level card with XP progress to the next level, the TLC card with distance
	and a check-in button, today's three quests with claim actions, and the
	pinned stat widget for the week.

	Reads GET /user/me for level, XP, streak and loggedToday, and the quest
	rotation for the day. The level card renders what the server sends; it
	does not recompute the curve.

ChallengesScreen    quests
	The featured challenge, then the browse list. Cards show the category,
	the XP reward, how many Lancers have joined, and the avatars of the three
	most recent joiners, which come from the backend's recentParticipants.
	Tapping a card opens the challenge sheet.

LogScreen           log
	The centre action. Daily steps against a goal with the weekly bar, then
	the facility areas, each opening its sub-activities. The catalogue is
	fetched from the backend and falls back to the static map in
	src/data/activityData.js if that call fails. A student can also log a
	custom activity, which becomes a per-user entry.

LeaderboardScreen   board
	Three tabs: Friends, Faculty, Campus. Podium for the top three, then the
	ranked list with avatar, flag, faculty and XP. Faculty and Campus are
	served by the backend leaderboard endpoints.

	The Friends tab is a leftover from a scope that has been dropped. See
	docs/maintenance.md.

ProfileScreen       profile
	Identity with the faculty crest, the link into the avatar journey, the
	badge shortcut, the live settings toggles for quest reminders and auto
	check-in, and sign out. Toggles write through services/settingsStore.js
	and take effect immediately.


Stack destinations
------------------

BadgesScreen        Badges
	Earned and unearned badges, with the locked ones shown rather than
	hidden so the ladder is legible. Gold text-only back button.

StatsScreen         Stats
	The stats index across logged exercises.

ExerciseStatsScreen ExerciseStats
	One exercise in detail: hero metric, range selector for week, month and
	year, bar chart and tiles. Backed by GET /stats/exercise/:key.

	Axis labels are range aware. Year shows three letter months, month shows
	the day of the month, day shows the hour. This is deliberate; a shared
	label format truncates and was a reported defect.

AvatarJourneyScreen avatarJourney
	The progression map. Five floating islands, one per tier, threaded by a
	single winding trail from Squire at the bottom to Lancer at the top. Each
	stop shows the real avatar art for that tier, the levels it covers and the
	XP needed to unlock it.

	Locked tiers stay visible behind a frosted scrim with a lock glyph rather
	than being hidden, so a student can see what they are working toward. The
	current tier carries a gold star, cleared tiers a check.

	Art only changes at a tier boundary. Sub-levels reuse the same art and are
	shown as rank pips.


Sheets
------

Sheets are modal surfaces rendered by components/Overlays.js rather than
screens, but they carry as much of the experience as some screens do.

	ChallengeSheet.js        challenge detail, live board, join and log
	ChallengeResultSheet.js  submit a supervised result for validation
	BadgeSheet.js            one badge in detail
	BadgeAwardModal.js       the celebration when a badge is awarded
	LevelUpModal.js          the celebration on level up

The sheet stack lifts with the keyboard through a keyboard listener that
translates the sheet by the keyboard height. A KeyboardAvoidingView does not
work for a bottom-pinned sheet; this was tried and reverted.